      en: "The Montegiardino Forestry Center is a forest management center in the municipality of Montegiardino, founded in 1995. It manages 300 hectares of forest, mainly oak and pine. The center produces 2,000 cubic meters of timber annually for construction and furniture. It engages in reforestation and biodiversity protection. It employs 40 foresters and offers environmental education programs. The forest hosts wild boar, roe deer, and stone martens. Montegiardino is the most forested area in San Marino, with 60% of its municipal area covered by forest. The center is FSC-certified.",
